  "_README": [
    "NHL injured / non-roster skaters -- players still with their club but left off the active roster",
    "the NHL web API returns once the season starts. Without this file a live roster refresh treats",
    "them as gone for all 82 games (the API roster is the ~23-man active list, not the organization).",
    "rosters.live_roster adds each one back to his team unless he is already on some team's active",
    "roster (returned from injury, or moved). rosters.live_toi then keeps him only if he played NHL",
    "5v5 minutes last season, at those minutes -- the same weight the backtest gives any opening-roster",
    "skater. That drops prospects and long-term absentees (no minutes last season) and mirrors the",
    "backtest's roster rule (a skater counts if he debuts within the team's first 20 games).",
    "Source: the league's opening-roster release (see source). Goalies and prospects with no NHL",
    "games are omitted (goalies are not in the skater model; prospects would not pass the minutes",
    "rule). Re-check this list whenever rosters are re-pulled. id = NHL player id."
  ],
